{"hash":"3fef17fbe6bfdadf","voice":"en-IN-NeerjaExpressiveNeural","rate":"+4%","dur":88.127,"said":"Stand here in the hall, beneath its dome, and imagine the moment Gautama’s long penance came to an end. Shiva appeared before him, pleased. ‘You have done no wrong,’ he said. ‘You were deceived. Those who harmed you are the sinners.’ And Gautama answered with a surprising gratitude: ‘Then they have done me a great kindness, Lord. Without them, how would I ever have seen you?’ Shiva offered him any boon he wished. Gautama asked nothing for himself. ‘Give us the Ganga, for the good of the world.’ And Ganga appeared, in the form of a woman. She would purify the sage, she said, and then return home. Shiva asked her to stay. Ganga replied that she would stay only if Shiva stayed here too, with Parvati. Then the gods made a promise of their own: every time Jupiter enters Leo, the sign of Simha, they would all come here to bathe in her. So Ganga stayed, and here she is called Gautami, the Godavari. And Shiva stayed, as Tryambaka, the three-eyed Lord. Now walk to the head of the steps that go down. The river, the Purana says, did not flow quietly at first.\n\nDid you know? Tryambaka, the ‘three-eyed one’, is the name of Shiva in the Mahamrityunjaya mantra: ‘Om Tryambakam yajamahe…’","segments":[{"key":"text","start":0,"end":1064},{"key":"didYouKnow","start":1080,"end":1190}],"words":[[0.098,0.445,0,5],[0.555,0.288,6,10],[0.855,0.096,11,13],[0.963,0.084,14,17],[1.06,0.385,18,22],[1.661,0.409,24,31],[2.081,0.168,32,35],[2.262,0.433,36,40],[2.899,0.168,42,45],[3.079,0.457,46,53],[3.548,0.084,54,57],[3.644,0.397,58,64],[4.052,0.661,65,74],[4.726,0.3,75,79],[5.038,0.385,80,87],[5.435,0.264,88,92],[5.711,0.12,93,95],[5.843,0.108,96,98],[5.963,0.3,99,102],[7.151,0.373,104,109],[7.536,0.385,110,118],[7.933,0.397,119,125],[8.341,0.312,126,129],[8.834,0.529,131,138],[10.276,0.144,141,144],[10.433,0.18,145,149],[10.625,0.252,150,154],[10.889,0.156,155,157],[11.058,0.493,158,163],[11.743